inese","Korean","Japanese","Portuguese - Brazil"],"min":[["OS","Windows 10 (64 bit only)"],["Processor","Intel i5-4460 / AMD Ryzen 5 1400"],["Memory","8 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Nvidia GeForce GTX 970 (4GB) / AMD RX 470 (4 GB)"],["DirectX","Version 12"],["Storage","20 GB available space"],["Sound Card","DirectX\u00ae compatible sound card with latest drivers"]],"rec":[["OS","Windows 10 (64 bit only)"],["Processor","Intel i7-4790 / AMD Ryzen 5 1600"],["Memory","8 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Nvidia GeForce GTX 1060 (6 GB) / AMD Radeon RX 570 (8 GB)"],["DirectX","Version 12"],["Storage","20 GB available space"],["Sound Card","DirectX\u00ae compatible sound card with latest drivers"]],"deck":3,"blurb":"Biking, skiing, snowboarding and wingsuit flying share one enormous map in Riders Republic, an open-world sports game built from urban streets and several U.S. national parks, among them Yosemite, Zion and the Grand Canyon. Players can switch between disciplines on the fly and take part in races, trick competitions and relaxed group rides alongside other riders online.\n\nLarge-scale races field more than fifty participants, and seasonal events add new sports and challenges over time. Cosmetic unlocks allow players to customize their rider's look. The game supports solo play, co-op and PvP, and it suits people who enjoy extreme sports and want variety in what they ride and how they compete."}}